<section class="sec" id="faq">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="fqg">
      <div class="fqh rv"><h2>Graphic design questions</h2><p>Can’t find what you need? Start a brief and a real person replies.</p><a class="btn btn-blue" href="#brief">Start your brief <svg aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-ne"/></svg></a></div>
      <article class="fqc rv" id="faq-what-counts-as-one-design-task"><button class="fqq" type="button" aria-expanded="false"><span>What counts as one design task?</span><i aria-hidden="true"></i></button><div class="fqx"><div><div class="pv"><div class="wg"><div class="wt"><span>One task</span><i><svg aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-pen"/></svg></i><i><svg aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-ne"/></svg></i></div><div class="gdf1"><span class="gdf1t"><img src="<?php echo NK_URI; ?>/assets/img/e33dc2874dcc.webp" alt=""></span><div><b>Raya poster</b><span><em>Format</em>Poster · A4</span><span><em>Message</em>Open house, Sat 11am–5pm</span></div></div></div></div><p>One task is one request with a defined format and message, such as a poster, a social post or a flyer. We finish it, you approve it, then the next request in your queue starts.</p></div></div></article><article class="fqc rv open" id="faq-how-do-unlimited-requests-work"><button class="fqq" type="button" aria-expanded="true"><span>How do unlimited requests work?</span><i aria-hidden="true"></i></button><div class="fqx"><div><div class="pv"><div class="wg"><div class="wt"><span>Active and queued</span><i><svg aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-sheet"/></svg></i><i><svg aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-ne"/></svg></i></div><div class="gdf2"><div><b>Essential</b><span class="gdf2a">1 active</span><span class="gdf2q"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><em>+ more</em></span></div><div class="on"><b>Studio</b><span class="gdf2a">2 active</span><span class="gdf2q"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><em>+ more</em></span></div></div></div></div><p>Add as many requests as you like. Essential works on 1 active task at a time and Studio on 2. The rest wait in your queue in the order you set.</p></div></div></article><article class="fqc rv" id="faq-how-fast-is-the-first-draft"><button class="fqq" type="button" aria-expanded="false"><span>How fast is the first draft?</span><i aria-hidden="true"></i></button><div class="fqx"><div><div class="pv"><div class="wg"><div class="wt"><span>Typical first draft</span><i><svg aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-cal"/></svg></i><i><svg aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-ne"/></svg></i></div><div class="gdf3"><p><b>Essential</b><span><i style="--w:100%"></i></span><em>2–3 days</em></p><p><b>Studio</b><span><i style="--w:55%"></i></span><em>1–2 days</em></p></div></div></div><p>A typical first draft takes 2–3 days on Essential and 1–2 days on Studio. Larger pieces, like a full deck, are agreed when you send the request.</p></div></div></article><article class="fqc rv" id="faq-how-many-revisions-do-i-get"><button class="fqq" type="button" aria-expanded="false"><span>How many revisions do I get?</span><i aria-hidden="true"></i></button><div class="fqx"><div><div class="pv"><div class="wg"><div class="wt"><span>Comment</span><i><svg aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-chat"/></svg></i><i><svg aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-ne"/></svg></i></div><div class="gdf4"><span class="pav2"><img src="<?php echo NK_URI; ?>/assets/img/7b1d80ea9991.jpg" alt=""></span><p><b>Mei</b><span>Can the date be bigger?</span></p><em class="pill g">Resolved in v2</em></div></div></div><p>Revisions within the agreed brief are included on every monthly plan. A new direction or an extra format is added to your queue as a new request.</p></div></div></article><article class="fqc rv" id="faq-can-i-order-just-one-design"><button class="fqq" type="button" aria-expanded="false"><span>Can I order just one design?</span><i aria-hidden="true"></i></button><div class="fqx"><div><div class="pv"><div class="wg"><div class="wt"><span>One-off artwork</span><i><svg aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-card"/></svg></i><i><svg aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-ne"/></svg></i></div><div class="gdf5"><span class="gdf5t"><img src="<?php echo NK_URI; ?>/assets/img/7805d5d69752.jpg" alt=""></span><div><small>Per artboard</small><b>RM120</b><span>Design + final export</span></div></div></div></div><p>Yes. One-off artwork is RM120 per artboard. You give the format and message, we design it and send the final export, with the review scope agreed up front.</p></div></div></article><article class="fqc rv" id="faq-do-you-design-logos-and-full-branding"><button class="fqq" type="button" aria-expanded="false"><span>Do you design logos and full branding?</span><i aria-hidden="true"></i></button><div class="fqx"><div><div class="pv"><div class="wg"><div class="wt"><span>What the plans cover</span><i><svg aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-tag"/></svg></i><i><svg aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-ne"/></svg></i></div><div class="gdf6"><div><small>Included</small><span>Social posts and posters</span><span>Flyers and collateral</span><span>Campaigns and decks · Studio</span></div><div class="x"><small>Quoted separately</small><span>Full brand identity</span><span>Filming</span><span>3D production</span></div></div></div></div><p>The plans cover everyday design using your existing brand. Complex branding, filming and 3D production are quoted separately.</p></div></div></article><article class="fqc rv" id="faq-what-files-do-i-get"><button class="fqq" type="button" aria-expanded="false"><span>What files do I get?</span><i aria-hidden="true"></i></button><div class="fqx"><div><div class="pv"><div class="wg"><div class="wt"><span>Final files</span><i><svg aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-send"/></svg></i><i><svg aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-ne"/></svg></i></div><div class="gdf7"><span><em class="p">PNG</em>Social and web</span><span><em>PDF</em>Print, with bleed</span><span><em class="j">JPG</em>WhatsApp and email</span></div></div></div><p>You get the final export for where the design is going: image files for social, web and WhatsApp, and print-ready PDF for printed pieces. Formats are agreed in each request.</p></div></div></article>
